WEBVTT

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.100
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.590
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.900
We're going to help out with Utau's concert today!

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.340
Well, I can help if there is any cleaning to do.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.900
I'm getting nervous for some reason!

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.510
You can do it! Go, go, Utau!

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:19.920
Doki!

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.640
You can do it! Go, go, Utau!

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.020
Doki!

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.410
Pyon Pyon

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.570
Fumu Fumu

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:36.480
Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.080
Howa Howa

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.280
Kira Kira

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.210
Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:42.970
What color is your egg?

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:45.750
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.790
Even if you say mean things,

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.640
I know you really love me.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:58.310
Even if we fight a lot,

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:01.980
it's just 'cause we're always together.

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:05.040
Because you believe in me,

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.800
I can do anything!

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:15.100
And that's why I unlock my heart!

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:20.810
The person you want to be; things you want to say.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:24.470
Important things; things that are true.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:28.180
Who you are; what you've yet to realize.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:31.830
Mysterious things; happy things.

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:36.740
All of these things are inside your egg!

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.880
Pyon Pyon

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.030
Fumu Fumu

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:42.970
Yeah! Yeah!

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:44.520
Howa Howa

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.730
Kira Kira

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:46.680
Yeah! Yeah!

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.420
What color is your egg?

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.230
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:00.600
Hey, Ikuto, shouldn't you be searching for the violin?

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.380
Could it've been those guys from Easter?

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.060
No, it's got to be them-nya!

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.500
Let's bust in there and take it back-nya!

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:12.290
No need to be scared-nya. If someone gets in our way, just Character Transform and kick their butt-nya!

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.060
I'm not scared.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:19.450
Who cares about the old man's violin, anyway?

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.930
It's been a while, Ikuto-kun.

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:28.920
I'm glad you've come here.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.560
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:34.060
Are you worried about something?

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:35.570
A sardine!

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.240
Do you always carry those around with you?

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:44.310
You never know when you might run into a wonderful little kitty cat, right?

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.970
How long do you plan to follow Easter's orders?

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.260
Or have you come to this place simply to stargaze? {And not talk about his worries, is how I understand it}

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.420
It's not like I can see any stars with all the smog covering the city.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:03.180
I suppose.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:09.300
But even if the stars are hidden behind thick clouds, they are surely still out there.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:13.680
Yet, though you understand this, you do not look up to the sky.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:18.730
If you were to one day lose sight of the stars, your heart would also become lost.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.500
Stop telling me things I already know.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:26.900
There they are, those wonderful cat ears!

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.900
I haven't been able to touch them in so long.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.520
This is always so much fun.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.810
I know you like cats, but this is a bit much.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:40.960
You really are a kitty cat.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:41.820
Don't play with me!

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.350
Let me play, too-nya!

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:49.350
Hoshina Utau! A Fresh Start!

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:49.350
Episode 59

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:55.350
Don't be embarrassed.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:04:02.640
My heartful song, my heartful song.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:04:02.640
My heartful song, my heartful song!

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.850
Hey, I can't hear Utau!

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:17.350
I'll sing forever, and wish for it to reach you.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.760
Jeez.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:11.100
No matter what you might say, you're still Utau's number one fan, huh?

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.810
What? That's not true.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.920
You are not being honest with yourself.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.980
And that's the part of you that's just like Utau.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.390
Don't lump us together!

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:26.100
And there we have it, a special performance at the shopping mall!

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:31.050
Next we'll feature the spot she appeared at...

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:32.520
Utau used to fill up huge concert halls.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.680
I hope she doesn't get down on herself.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.600
Yeah.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:41.930
Utau's tough. Though, I guess I am sort of worried.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:43.640
Is that so?

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.140
Where did <i>you</i> come from?

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:47.900
What a miserable aura.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:49.300
It is quite frightening.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.250
Did something bad happen?

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.350
No, actually, something really wonderful.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:59.770
Utau-chan's hard work has been recognized, and she can now sing at a live concert.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.630
That's great!

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:02.870
Then why are you...

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:08.130
I just can't stop worrying!

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:11.820
Utau-chan was once sought out by the entertainment world.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:15.600
But she was cast aside by her fans, and has now fallen to the deepest depths.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:21.380
I'm sure that inside her heart, she has lost confidence and is frightened!

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.270
And so!

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:26.720
I want you all to come help make this concert really rock!

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.170
But...

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:31.550
There's no time for indecision!

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:33.170
The concert is tonight!

00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:34.360
Tonight?

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:37.950
In 4 hours, 56 minutes, 23 seconds, to be precise.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:39.730
Why is she so obsessed with this?

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:40.590
But...

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:42.300
What do you mean, but?

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.230
It's about Utau.

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:47.640
You'll just get in the way. You're annoying.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:50.530
That's definitely what she'd say.

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:51.960
Amu-chan!

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.970
And you call yourself Utau-chan's best friend?

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:57.220
I don't remember calling her my...

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:01.680
"Utau's tough. Though, I guess I am sort of worried."

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:04.650
Was that all a lie, then?!

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:07.770
Liars will burn in Hell.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.530
It does sound kind of fun, you know.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:13.410
Yes, let us help.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:16.430
Go, go! Let's go! Utau!

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:19.380
Uh, it's not your concert, you know.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:21.930
So you've decided to come, right, Amu-chan?

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:25.270
Utau-chan is counting on this concert!

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:27.620
All right.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.140
Amu-chan!

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:32.850
But how can we make it really rock?

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:35.720
I've got it!

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:41.930
Today's Live Performance: Hoshina Utau

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:44.930
You'll just get in the way. You're annoying.

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:46.390
I knew you'd say that.

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:49.130
That's right! Stop meddling!

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.430
I was just thinking about Utau-chan's-

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.720
That's what I meant by meddling!

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:58.440
And you guys came to make a mess of Utau's concert, right?

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.010
No, we didn't.

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:01.350
You suck.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:04.850
As a pro, I've always taken the lead.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:07.210
I don't need your help, Amu.

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:09.680
Well then, instead of me,

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.470
maybe Ikuto could help?

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:12.430
Ikuto?

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:14.160
What about Ikuto?

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.140
Will he come?

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:21.970
I haven't actually asked him yet, but I was thinking it might be nice for him to play his violin at your concert.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:26.260
See? I think it's a good idea.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:27.490
Ikuto!

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.680
She's not listening.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:33.970
Utau hasn't seen Ikuto in a while. She's going through withdrawal.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.010
Utau-chan, we're gonna start the rehearsal!

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:41.100
Utau-chan, I'd like to do a lighting check!

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:43.010
We're doing a sound check!

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:44.770
Utau-chan!

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:45.930
I know.

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:49.990
Can you check the song order?

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:52.920
What if we insert this song here?

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:54.600
Yeah, that sounds interesting.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:57.530
I don't think Utau's going anywhere.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:58.390
Yeah.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:08.850
But even if the stars are hidden behind thick clouds, they are surely still out there.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:13.410
Yet, though you understand this, you do not look up to the sky.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:17.470
Ikuto!

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:23.600
I knew you'd be here.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.960
You always play your violin here, so...

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:28.660
Do you want something-nya?

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:30.760
I have a little favor to ask.

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:32.260
A favor?

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:36.220
I'd like you to play your violin at Utau's concert tonight.

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:40.580
I thought you were going to say something interesting. Guess not.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:43.350
This is Utau's first concert since she went independent.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:46.430
I'm sure she wants you to be there to support her, Ikuto.

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:47.410
I'll pass.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:54.740
Utau really wanted to come ask you in person, but she has to get ready for the concert, so...

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:57.430
She's really working hard!

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:58.270
So...

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:00.200
You're really persistent, aren't you-nya?

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:03.060
How is he supposed to play without a violin-nya?

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:07.450
Oh yeah, where is your violin?

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:09.640
It was stolen!

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:09.640
Yoru!

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:12.050
Stolen?

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:14.640
So back then...

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:20.220
As if someone like you, who doesn't treasure anything, could understand!

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:24.160
I didn't know. I'm sorry.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:27.260
Wait!

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:32.260
Do you know what happened to it? I'll help look.

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:38.260
It's none of your business.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:41.150
There's also Utau's concert, so...

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:44.080
I hate the violin.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.760
Well, I love it! I love hearing you play!

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:54.100
It gives me such a warm feeling, and whenever I hear it, I feel like I can be honest with myself.

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:59.820
Someone who hates the violin wouldn't be able to make people feel like that!

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:03.640
It's only because you're a simpleton.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:07.660
At least say you'll come to Utau's concert, okay?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:08.640
No, thanks.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:11.650
You don't understand anything, Ikuto!

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:14.390
You stubborn, hard-headed, good-for-nothing jerk!

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:18.570
Is that really the way to ask someone for a favor?

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:24.390
Maybe if you tried asking a bit more sweetly...

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.850
What does he mean by sweetly?

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.390
Does he want a kiss?

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:31.030
A meeting of the lips?

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:32.260
It's love!

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:35.050
The love flag has been raised!

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.430
I must report this to Utau-chan!

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:38.430
You can't!

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.580
I won't be tempted.

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:15.000
Are you an idiot?!

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.470
I'll never ask you for a favor again!

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:20.140
Jeez, what's <i>with</i> him?!

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:25.060
Man, if you hadn't done that, she'd never have given up-nya.

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:29.600
She doesn't get that you're keeping your distance from Utau on purpose, so she doesn't end up

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:31.410
getting used by Easter again-nya.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:33.930
What is it-nya?

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:38.430
Easter?

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:42.430
The plan is progressing well.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:49.070
Whether Ikuto's violin or Lulu will yield results first...

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:55.140
Either way, it will not be long until the Embryo is delivered to you, Boss.

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:57.970
I'll be expecting it.

00:11:57.970 --> 00:11:58.790
Yes, Sir.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:08.310
The violin's got to be here at Easter.

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:12.780
But if you get it back, will you play at Utau's concert?

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:14.230
No.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:20.710
Looks like we'll have to do another simulation.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:23.100
Hey, could you bring in that violi-

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:26.600
Tsu-Tsukiyomi Ikuto!

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.100
Chief!

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.140
You guys!

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:35.390
Didn't you hear him? He told you to bring the violin.

00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:38.760
We've got no choice! Do what he says!

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:44.060
H-H-Hey!

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:48.120
They don't value your life very much-nya.

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:54.980
What is the meaning of this?

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:56.930
There's an intruder in the research labs!

00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:57.760
What?

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.090
Give me the violin!

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:05.510
I can't! Without the key from the Director, I can't...

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.350
That way!

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:21.780
We totally lost them-nya.

00:13:36.470 --> 00:13:38.320
I am so mad right now.

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:41.100
Just calm down.

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:44.010
Right. Even without Ikuto...

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:48.820
We can rock the concert ourselves!

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:51.390
Yay! Utau!

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:02.950
I guess Ikuto isn't coming, huh?

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.930
It's not like I was waiting for him.

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:17.720
Amu! Where's Ikuto? You brought him with you, right?

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:22.050
Utau, he told me he wasn't coming.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:25.390
I'm sorry.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:30.080
Why are you apologizing, Amu?

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:33.850
W-Why?

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:41.310
Oh, um, because...

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:43.350
Hinamori Amu!

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.810
Did you come to support Utau?

00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:46.690
Sanjo-san.

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:48.820
I guess even you have your good points!

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.820
Well, since you're here and all...

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:52.710
Please hand out these flyers!

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:56.260
We have no money for advertising, you know.

00:14:56.260 --> 00:14:58.860
It's really hard to bring in an audience!

00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:01.060
Okay, thanks a million!

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:11.220
You're finally having a concert, so why won't Ikuto come?

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.760
And El went off somewhere, too.

00:15:20.090 --> 00:15:24.920
Well, you don't need Ikuto. You'll do just fine on your own, right, Utau?

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:26.110
That's right.

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:30.430
I decided to do this myself.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:33.310
I can't keep relying on Ikuto forever.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:36.430
Isn't that right, Il?

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:40.180
I'm glad you understand.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:42.870
Utau's really changed, hasn't she?

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:43.460
Yeah.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:45.290
She is wonderful!

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:52.600
This isn't good.

00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:55.030
I need to work harder.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.950
There's hardly anyone here.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:04.560
Please take one!

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.260
Please take one!

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:08.250
Please take one!

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:09.220
Please take one!

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:12.910
Hoshina Utau's concert will be starting soon!

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:14.180
Please come watch!

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:16.650
Amu-chan!

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:21.930
Utau wants to do this, so we've got to get a ton of people to listen to her.

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:25.620
Hoshina Utau is singing at a concert!

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:27.140
Please take one!

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:28.850
Please take one!

00:16:28.850 --> 00:16:30.560
Please take one!

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:31.850
Plea-

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:35.720
Shoot.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.600
Tadase-kun?

00:16:48.890 --> 00:16:49.980
Why are you...

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:53.680
Rima, Yaya? Why is everyone here?

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.380
Isn't it obvious?

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:58.320
You can't do it all by yourself, Amu-chan.

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:00.760
So I asked them to help you!

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:04.110
We'll lend a hand, Hinamori-san.

